[57.821742, "o", "9:def measure_ref_program_time(\r\n12:    num_warmup: int = 5,\r\n13:    num_trials: int = 100,\r\n15:    timing_method: str = \"cuda_event\",\r\n82:                # the warmup in the timing function handles that and should not affect timed trials\r\n97:                num_warmup=num_warmup,\r\n98:                num_trials=num_trials,\r\n114:def measure_program_time(*args, **kwargs):\r\n126:def clear_l2_cache(device: torch.device | str = \"cuda\"):\r\n144:def clear_l2_cache_triton(cache=None, device: str = \"cuda\"):\r\n155:def get_timing_function(\r\n156:    method: str = \"cuda_event\", # by default \r\n162:        - \"cuda_event\": torch.cuda.event timing (default, explicit trial control)\r\n171:        Timing function with signature (kernel_fn, args, num_warmup, num_trials, \r\n179:        case \"cuda_event\":\r\n180:            return time_execution_with_cuda_event\r\n201:def time_execution_with_cuda_event(\r\n204:    num_warmup: int = 3,\r\n205:    num_trials: int = 10,\r\n222:        num_warmup: Number of warmup iterations before timing\r\n223:       "]
[57.821773, "o", " num_trials: Number of timing trials to run\r\n229:        List of elapsed times in milliseconds (length = num_trials)\r\n239:        for _ in range(num_warmup):\r\n246:        print(f\"[Profiling] Using device: {device} {torch.cuda.get_device_name(device)}, warm up {num_warmup}, trials {num_trials}\"\r\n252:        for trial in range(num_trials + discard_first):\r\n256:            start_event = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)\r\n257:            end_event = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)\r\n284:def time_execution_with_do_bench_interface(\r\n288:    num_warmup: int = 3, \r\n289:    num_trials: int = 10,\r\n296:    Uses Triton's adaptive benchmarking with fixed time budgets (warmup=25ms, rep=100ms) [Triton do_bench default].\r\n299:    Note: num_warmup, num_trials, discard_first are ignored - included only for \r\n305:        num_warmup: (ignored) Triton controls warmup\r\n306:        num_trials: (ignored) Triton controls trial count  \r\n326:            warmup=25,\r\n333:def time_execution_with_do_bench_impl(\r\n336:    num_warmup: "]
[57.821788, "o", "int = 3,\r\n337:    num_trials: int = 10,\r\n347:    to use num_warmup and num_trials that explicitly follows what user define here\r\n348:    instead of do_bench's version that computes how many times to run warmup and \r\n"]
